PRETABLE_3 -- pvrrenderexit, test-variant table 3 (repair 3: the class closure completed; 91 rows).  Written BEFORE table 3
runs: its mtime must precede every RESULT file in table3/ (the frozen probe is copied there first and is older).  Instrument:
table3/probe91_frozen.py, cmp-identical to regress/pvr_zwrite_probe.py when this was written (91/91 on build/ in base91/).
Baseline: dev_pvr.c.fix3 (== GXEMUL-SEC src/devices/dev_pvr.c == ../det_20261104/dev_pvr.c.fix).  Variants: pvr_variants_3.py.
EVERY prediction is EXACT -- the full red set, none = all 91 green -- except Y2s/Y2t/Y4s/Y4t (undefined behaviour, NOT
PREDICTED, counted in no tally).  Old rows: table 2's MEASURED red set (the 68 rows carry over unchanged); the 23 new rows:
DERIVED (CLOSURE3.md).  114 variants: 110 predicted, 105 predicted red, 5 predicted green (EQUIVALENT), 4 NOT PREDICTED.
Legs: base 91/91 CONTROL=OK SYMPTOM=ABSENT; HEAD (det_20261104/dev_pvr.c.HEAD, the exit) 58/91 SYMPTOM=PRESENT CONTROL=OK --
table 2's 26 plus the seven new rows whose sessions carry a Z-off header and so end the process (zeq, texzeq, maskoff, zleft x2,
texzleft x2): MEASURED already, r3_20261105/head91/; null media CONTROL=FAIL: /bin/true 9/91 (only the nine `session` rows,
which want exit 0), an absent binary 0/91, /bin/false 1/91 (`neg apparatus`).
CHANNELS of the 23 new rows (each row's variants and the observable that differs; derivations in CLOSURE3.md):
  swap s before (364,180) BLACK -- A: SWAP row 180 starts at 365.0 after its swap; `x1 - 1` draws 364 red.
  swap s tip (400,249) RED -- B: row 249 arrives 400.5 / 399.5; `x1 > x2 + 1` leaves it reversed: nothing drawn.
  swap vert (300,150) GREEN -- C: VERT row 150 arrives 300.0 / 300.0, start end green (v1), stop end red (v2): `>=` swaps to red.
  swap frac past (151,101) BLACK -- I: FRAC row 101 ends at 150.5; `x < x2 + 1` draws 151.
  texswap s before / s tip / vert -- A / B / C through texturedline (int ends; VERT's start end u 0.5 = the green texel).
  ramp l end (440,60) GREEN -- the swap body: RAMP row 60 arrives 520.0 (v1: z 1.0, magenta) / 440.0 (v2: z 2.0, green); COVER
    (z 1.5, blue, after) fails at 440.  No z exchange: blue.  No r / g / b exchange: 0xffe0 / 0x0000 / 0x07ff.
  texramp l end (440,60) BLUE -- texturedline: v2's (u,v) (0, 0.125) = texel (0,1), stored blue.  No z exchange: COVER's red;
    no u exchange: texel (4,1), never stored, 0x0000; no v exchange: texel (0,0), red.
  edges2 l rev (1,230) RED -- D: LREV row 230 arrives 30.0 / -30.0 (x1 >= 0, x2 < 0); `(x2 < 0 && x2 < 0)` returns early.
  edges2 r rev (639,400) RED -- E and R2: RREV row 400 arrives 700.0 / 639.0; `(x1 >= xsize && x1 >= xsize)` and
    `x2 >= xsize - 1` return early.
  texedges2 l rev / r rev -- D / E / R2 through texturedline.
  edges2 l tip (1,259) RED -- W3: LREV row 259 arrives 1.0 / -1.0, swapped it draws column 1; `x1 < d->bytes_per_pixel` (2)
    returns early.  texedges2 l tip: the same through texturedline (ints 1 / -1).
  zleft row 0 (1,0) RED -- W1, W2: Z-OFF ZCORNER row 0 spans 1.0..31.0; `x > d->zwrite_disabled` drops column 1 and `y <
    d->zwrite_disabled` drops row 0, for Z-off polygons only.  texzleft row 0: textured.
  zleft tip (1,159) RED -- W4: Z-off LEFT3 row 159 spans -1.0..1.0, forward; `x2 < d->bytes_per_pixel` returns early.
    texzleft tip: textured.
  zeq overlap (220,180) GREEN -- F: a Z-off T2 at z 2.0 over T1's stored 2.0 passes `<=`; F refuses it.  texzeq: textured.
  maskoff overlap (220,180) GREEN -- G: header word 1 0x0c000000; `& 1` disables T1's store, `== 1` does not.
  maskhi overlap (220,180) RED -- H, H9, H17, H33: header word 1 0xf0000000; `& 1` keeps T1's store, `& 5/9/17/33` drop it.

